# Cloudflare Pages headers - ports the old nginx security/cache config.
# Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# NOTE: Pages *appends* a header from every matching rule (it does not
# override). So Cache-Control is set on non-overlapping asset rules only -
# never in /* - to avoid concatenated, conflicting values. HTML pages fall
# back to the Pages default cache behaviour.
#
# CSP and GA4: the analytics allowances below are deliberate, not incidental.
#   *.google-analytics.com   GA4 routes hits to regionN.google-analytics.com
#                            based on visitor location. The old policy named
#                            region1 only, so visitors routed anywhere else
#                            had their hits blocked outright.
#   analytics.google.com     second collection endpoint GA4 fires alongside
#   stats.g.doubleclick.net  Google Signals: cross-device and demographics
#   www.google.com           Google Signals, same purpose
#
# Still blocked on purpose: the ga-audiences remarketing pixel, which fires
# against the visitor's local Google domain (www.google.com.sg, .co.uk, and
# so on). CSP has no wildcard for top-level domains, so allowing it properly
# would mean enumerating every ccTLD. It only feeds Google Ads remarketing
# audiences and has no effect on measurement. If the console noise is
# irritating, turn Google Signals off in GA4 rather than widening this.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'unsafe-eval' https://www.googletagmanager.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; img-src 'self' data: https://www.googletagmanager.com https://*.google-analytics.com https://stats.g.doubleclick.net https://www.google.com; font-src 'self' data: https://fonts.gstatic.com; connect-src 'self' https://*.google-analytics.com https://analytics.google.com https://stats.g.doubleclick.net https://www.google.com https://cloudflareinsights.com;
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=()

# Long-lived static assets (mirrors the nginx expires 1y block). Each asset
# matches exactly one of these extension rules, so Cache-Control stays clean.
/*.css
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.js
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.woff
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.woff2
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.ttf
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.jpg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.jpeg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.gif
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*.svg
